{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","commitSha":"c2534ff9c84422e00711da31629a76f3f59feb98","shard":"65af60195a7d601f","symbols":[{"path":"xrpl/ClosureCounter","kind":"class","name":"ClosureCounter","qualifiedName":"xrpl::ClosureCounter","scope":"xrpl","category":"production","access":"public","documentation":{"status":"present","brief":[{"type":"text","text":"The role of a "},{"type":"code","text":"ClosureCounter"},{"type":"text","text":" is to assist in shutdown by letting callers wait for the completion of closures (of a specific type signature) that they previously registered."}],"description":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"These closures are typically callbacks for asynchronous operations. The lifetime of a "},{"type":"code","text":"ClosureCounter"},{"type":"text","text":" consists of two phases: the initial expanding \"fork\" phase, and the subsequent shrinking \"join\" phase."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In the fork phase, callers register a closure by passing the closure and receiving a substitute in return. The substitute has the same callable interface as the closure, and it informs the "},{"type":"code","text":"ClosureCounter"},{"type":"text","text":" whenever it is copied or destroyed, so that it can keep an accurate count of copies."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The transition to the join phase is made by a call to "},{"type":"code","text":"join"},{"type":"text","text":". In this phase, every substitute returned going forward will be null, signaling to the caller that they should drop the closure and cancel their operation. "},{"type":"code","text":"join"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks until all existing closure substitutes are destroyed."}]}],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/core/ClosureCounter.h","line":37},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/core/ClosureCounter.h","line":38,"endLine":209}},"corre